From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: draw a child's parent background at the child's position

Purpose: draw a transparent toolbar's buttons over the right background
when only some of them are repainted.
XP behavior: DrawThemeParentBackground offsets the DC by the child's
position in its parent and only clips to the rectangle, which is in the
child's coordinates: tests/theme-parent-background.c on the reference XP
gives the parent the viewport origin -30,-20 for a child at 30,20, both
without a rectangle and with (40,5)-(60,15).
Wine before: the origin was the rectangle's position in the parent
(-70,-25), so a partial repaint got the wrong part of the parent. XP's
folder window has a transparent toolbar on a rebar, which repaints a
button with its rectangle when its state changes: Move To and Copy To,
disabled when a window opened inactive was activated, were drawn on black
(in the test VM every time).
Change: offset by the child's origin in the parent; the rectangle still
clips.
Evidence: the probe gives XP's origins. In the test VM, the two buttons
kept the toolbar's background in 4 tries of 4 (black in every try
before). 13 scenes of the English XP session (Luna), the taskbar
included, are unchanged.
Scope: all applications (documented behavior).
---
 dlls/uxtheme/draw.c | 15 +++++----------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
index 932d8c9..5551cce 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
@@ -155,8 +155,7 @@ static BOOL external_shell_taskbar_background(HWND hwnd, HDC dc, const RECT *cli
  */
 HRESULT WINAPI DrawThemeParentBackground(HWND hwnd, HDC hdc, RECT *prc)
 {
-    RECT rt;
-    POINT org;
+    POINT org, origin = {0, 0};
     HWND hParent;
     HRGN clip = NULL;
     int hasClip = -1;
@@ -167,9 +166,6 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DrawThemeParentBackground(HWND hwnd, HDC hdc, RECT *prc)
     if(!hParent)
         hParent = hwnd;
     if(prc) {
-        rt = *prc;
-        MapWindowPoints(hwnd, hParent, (LPPOINT)&rt, 2);
-
         clip = CreateRectRgn(0,0,1,1);
         hasClip = GetClipRgn(hdc, clip);
         if(hasClip == -1)
@@ -177,12 +173,11 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DrawThemeParentBackground(HWND hwnd, HDC hdc, RECT *prc)
         else
             IntersectClipRect(hdc, prc->left, prc->top, prc->right, prc->bottom);
     }
-    else {
-        GetClientRect(hwnd, &rt);
-        MapWindowPoints(hwnd, hParent, (LPPOINT)&rt, 2);
-    }
 
-    OffsetViewportOrgEx(hdc, -rt.left, -rt.top, &org);
+    /* The parent paints at the child's position; the rectangle, in the
+     * child's coordinates, only clips (tests/theme-parent-background.c on XP). */
+    MapWindowPoints(hwnd, hParent, &origin, 1);
+    OffsetViewportOrgEx(hdc, -origin.x, -origin.y, &org);
 
     SendMessageW(hParent, WM_ERASEBKGND, (WPARAM)hdc, 0);
     SendMessageW(hParent, WM_PRINTCLIENT, (WPARAM)hdc, PRF_CLIENT);
